# The committed blobs are LF. The Python gates read with Path.read_text(), which
# applies universal-newline translation, so they were already CRLF-safe. Node is not:
# readFileSync returns the bytes, so the install component test's LF-only frontmatter
# regex failed on a Windows checkout under core.autocrlf=true and passed on the ubuntu
# runners in CI. That test now normalises on read; this keeps the tree matching CI so
# the next LF assumption does not have to be found the same way.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises to LF in the index (what autocrlf already did) and
# also checks out LF on every platform, so the tree matches what CI sees. It adds no
# phantom modifications to an existing CRLF tree: git normalises on read before
# diffing, so those files still compare equal to the index.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
